{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2137-12-06 20:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. ___. I'm Dr. ___, one of your hospital doctors. You've just come up from the procedure suite after your bronchoscopy and dilation. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2137-12-06 20:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, doctor. I’m okay. My throat hurts, maybe a 6 out of 10. But it’s better since I got the pain medicine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2137-12-06 20:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. The bronchoscopy can cause some irritation and soreness. We’ll keep the oxycodone available for you as needed. You’re breathing well, and your trach is stable. Any chest pain or trouble breathing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2137-12-06 20:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just the throat pain. No shortness of breath. I feel pretty comfortable sitting up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2137-12-06 20:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We did a balloon dilation to open up some narrow areas in your airway, which is part of your ongoing care for the tracheal stenosis. We also cleaned out some secretions and removed a small pseudomembrane. Biopsies were taken to check for inflammation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2137-12-06 20:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Was anything abnormal in the biopsy? Or the washings?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2137-12-06 20:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The initial report shows inflammation and granulation tissue, which is expected. No signs of infection or cancer. The bronchial wash showed lots of white blood cells, which means there’s inflammation, but no organisms were seen on the gram stain yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2137-12-06 20:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember last time we found Pseudomonas. Could it be back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2137-12-06 20:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The culture is still growing. There’s a gram-negative rod, but we won’t know exactly what it is for a few days. If it’s an infection, we’ll adjust treatment, but right now you’re not showing signs of active infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2137-12-06 20:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2137-12-06 20:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at this point. Your vitals are stable, you’re not spiking a fever, and your breathing is good. The main issue right now is post-procedure pain, which we’re managing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2137-12-06 20:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the steroids? Last time I was on a higher dose after the procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2137-12-06 20:41:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. We’re starting you on prednisone 50 mg daily for five days to reduce airway inflammation from the procedure. Then you’ll go back to your usual 7.5 mg daily after that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2137-12-06 20:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my other meds—methotrexate, famotidine—should I keep those?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2137-12-06 20:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue all your home medications. We’ve listed them in your chart. Methotrexate for your relapsing polychondritis, famotidine for reflux, and your calcium and vitamin D."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2137-12-07 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You did well overnight. Your breathing stayed stable, and the chest X-ray shows no complications like a pneumothorax. The trach tube is in a good position."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2137-12-07 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good to hear. So I can go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2137-12-07 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, if everything stays the same. We’ll discharge you later this morning. You’ll need to follow up with Dr. ___ in interventional pulmonology in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2137-12-07 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I start feeling worse—like more pain or trouble breathing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2137-12-07 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call your doctor or come back if you develop fever, chills, increased secretions, or worsening shortness of breath. Otherwise, keep taking the prednisone as prescribed and rest at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2137-12-07 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do that. Thanks for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2137-12-07 08:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll get your discharge papers ready, including a small supply of oxycodone for breakthrough pain. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2137-12-07 08:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate it, doctor. Feels good to be going home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2137-12-07 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ve tolerated the procedure well and recovered quickly. Just keep an eye on how you feel over the next few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2137-12-07 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. And I’ll call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2137-12-07 08:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Your rheumatology team also knows about this admission, so no changes to your methotrexate. Stay hydrated and keep using your humidifier."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2137-12-07 08:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I always do. That humidifier’s been a lifesaver since last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2137-12-07 08:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Glad to hear it. We’ll have the nurse go over your discharge instructions one more time before you leave. Take it easy, and we’ll see you in clinic soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2137-12-06 20:17:00",
    "admission_end": "2137-12-07 15:27:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted for post-procedural monitoring after undergoing a flexible bronchoscopy with balloon dilation for recurrent tracheal stenosis related to relapsing polychondritis. He experienced throat pain post-procedure, which was managed with oxycodone. He remained stable throughout the admission with no respiratory compromise. A short course of prednisone was initiated to reduce airway inflammation. Bronchial washings showed gram-negative rods pending culture, but no acute infection was evident. He was discharged home the following morning with instructions to follow up in interventional pulmonology and to complete the steroid taper.",
    "problems": [
      "Bronchitis, not specified as acute or chronic",
      "Other acute postprocedural pain",
      "Pain in throat",
      "Chest pain, unspecified",
      "Chronic respiratory failure, unspecified whether with hypoxia or hypercapnia",
      "Relapsing polychondritis",
      "Ruvalcaba-Myhre-Smith syndrome",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Tracheostomy status"
    ]
  }
}
